WEBVTT

00:03.880 --> 00:04.280
All right.

00:04.280 --> 00:09.120
So with that we have covered 13 different date and time functions in SQL.

00:09.120 --> 00:13.800
So we have learned how to extract the date parts using seven different functions.

00:13.800 --> 00:16.000
And we have learned as well when to use which one.

00:16.000 --> 00:20.240
So they are amazing in order to do that aggregations and as well filtering.

00:20.240 --> 00:25.360
And then we have learned how to change the date format from one to another and as well how to change

00:25.360 --> 00:26.280
the data types.

00:26.280 --> 00:29.920
And then we learned how to do mathematical operations on our dates.

00:29.920 --> 00:37.160
So how we can add or subtract days, years, months from a date or the amazing function that date diff

00:37.200 --> 00:41.600
where we can go and find the differences in days or years between two days.

00:41.640 --> 00:46.640
And the last one, we can go and validate whether the values that we have are dates or not.

00:46.640 --> 00:52.440
So as we learned, date functions are amazing functions in order to do data analysis and reporting.

00:52.440 --> 00:53.240
All right my friends.

00:53.240 --> 00:58.480
So with that, we have learned a lot of very important SQL functions on how to manipulate the date and

00:58.480 --> 01:00.880
